WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.400
Film Courage: I would imagine this comes up
a lot.

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:09.372
If I write Hollyshorts a letter “I would
love it if you can waive the [film festival

00:00:09.372 --> 00:00:15.730
submission] fee and I will do this…this…this…to
reciprocate for that money.”

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.380
Are you able to then take my submission and
waive that fee?

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.529
Daniel Sol, Co-Founder of the Hollyshorts
Film Festival: My answer to that would be

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:23.529
“No.”

00:00:23.529 --> 00:00:28.750
Yes, we are not a fan of fee-waiver requests.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:37.570
Many festivals probably agree with me, maybe
some don’t offer a lot of waivers.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:42.340
The only instance is if I go to a festival
and I see your film and say I’ve got to

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.340
have it.

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:45.070
If I’m essentially at your door begging
you for your film then obviously in fairness

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:47.460
I’m telling you to submit.

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:49.390
Worse case offer you a discount or waive the
fee.

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:54.410
But I don’t really do that anymore, we don’t
ask for films really at all.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:01:00.090
It’s not about the financial aspect, it’s
about the fairness of the process.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:04.071
If you feel your film is worthy of that, well
many others are too.

00:01:04.071 --> 00:01:08.560
So why are we waiving one fee just because
you asked for it and everyone else is paying

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:09.560
full price.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:10.890
What’s the difference?

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:14.050
Why should I offer you this nice gift?

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.260
For what?

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.790
Just to ask for it is not a good enough reason.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:24.310
Even if there are extenuating situations or
we hear all sort of stuff whether it’s financial

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:27.320
stuff obviously for student filmmakers.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:32.590
Obviously money is tight, you’re in college,
you’re a student, I get that part.

00:01:32.590 --> 00:01:37.320
You have to pick which festival you are going
to submit to and you have to make a plan.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.960
You’ve got to just make something happen.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.729
You can’t just say I want a fee waiver because
I’m having some struggles.

00:01:42.729 --> 00:01:44.300
We all have struggles, we all have things.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:45.300
I was in college and broke.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:46.910
I had to pay for certain things that I wanted.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:48.470
You have to make it happen.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:52.270
You don’t just ask for it because you feel
you deserve it.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:55.310
To me there is a certain element…it’s
offensive.

00:01:55.310 --> 00:01:58.720
I personally don’t like it.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.860
I will try to answer as many as I can.

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:04.210
I tell people we just do not take waivers
and that’s it.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:08.509
At times if there are certain times where
we like the email and someone is making a

00:02:08.509 --> 00:02:13.420
good effort, there’s a real reason behind
something or whatever I don’t know we can

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:16.810
always say look there are certain situations
where we have discounts with promo partners

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:17.810
and things.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:21.980
Look them up and if they send their code out
and if they have a discount there, you have

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:22.980
a discount.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:23.980
But that’s all we can do, you still have
to pay.

00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:27.980
It’s still the principal of it, everybody
is submitting and paying.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:31.850
So if you get accepted and you don’t pay
and then they paid their money and they didn’t

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:37.560
get in or they got in why are you getting
the same equal benefit?

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:43.170
Every dollar counts but it’s not like you
are submitting $500.00 to submit to a festival.

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:47.130
Now it adds up for a lot of festivals, I get
that.

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.130
Our fee is what our fee is.

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:50.250
I don’t care what other festivals charge
or how many other festivals you’re submitting

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:51.250
to.

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.930
For us we look at it as you should submit
to ours.

00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:59.380
We feel it’s in that caliber and it’s
in the range of $35.00 to $70 or so dollar

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.430
range of early to late.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:02.150
If you submit it on the last day, it’s higher.

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:06.020
If you submit to early bird it’s anywhere
from $35 to $40 dollars.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:11.370
It’s not something you will need to donate
blood for.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.430
And again, I don’t want to come across as
too flippant or anything.

00:03:13.430 --> 00:03:20.819
It’s just to me is something that takes
time from my day or any of our days, or interns

00:03:20.819 --> 00:03:25.930
or assistants to answer these emails, which
some of them we can’t even catch up on.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:30.550
Or some of them we wonder why even bother
answering, like do I have to answer you?

00:03:30.550 --> 00:03:34.270
I don’t have to but we are trying to at
least be kind enough to get back to you and

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:35.950
say “Look we just don’t offer waivers.”

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:46.071
It’s not even a time thing, it’s a principal
thing like why is everyone else paying and

00:03:46.071 --> 00:03:49.270
what makes you different and feel you’re
more special that you don’t have to pay?

00:03:49.270 --> 00:03:58.120
Based on not just struggle but just my film
is that good…and that bugs me even more!

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:02.590
Filmmakers should never reference “I played
at this festival, that festival so that means

00:04:02.590 --> 00:04:05.379
obviously I’m at a certain place, I’ve
gotten into some festivals.

00:04:05.379 --> 00:04:08.390
But now waive my fee for this one.”

00:04:08.390 --> 00:04:11.709
Okay, let me ask you this, did you submit
to those festivals and pay?

00:04:11.709 --> 00:04:12.940
Yeah right…yes you did.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.459
I’m assuming yes.

00:04:14.459 --> 00:04:19.049
So okay now you’re telling me my festival
is not worthy of submitting the fee and paying.

00:04:19.049 --> 00:04:22.090
You got into those festivals…do you see
the hypocrisy of that?

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:23.449
That bugs me to no end.

00:04:23.449 --> 00:04:27.009
You’re telling me you’ve played these
festivals already so obviously we can assume

00:04:27.009 --> 00:04:29.710
you paid the submission fee, I highly doubt
they gave you the waivers.

00:04:29.710 --> 00:04:31.870
And at times I would actually get mad and
I used to say it to people.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.659
I would say “Oh so did you pay this fee?”

00:04:33.659 --> 00:04:34.969
No answer.

00:04:34.969 --> 00:04:37.440
You paid their fee, so you’re telling me
now you’re not going to pay our submission

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:42.139
fee at a moderate rate because you played
there already and you just don’t want to

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:43.139
pay our fee.

00:04:43.139 --> 00:04:47.289
Do you not inherently notice how offensive
that can be to a festival?

00:04:47.289 --> 00:04:51.050
You’re telling me we played them first but
it’s going to be personal.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.910
You’re telling me you played there and paid
there and you don’t want to pay for us.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:55.690
You’re saying now you ran out of money and
you don’t want to pay?

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:56.690
Or you don’t want to pay period?

00:04:56.690 --> 00:05:03.069
Or you are going to ask for something because
you have some more special thing going because

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:04.539
you’ve been accepted.

00:05:04.539 --> 00:05:05.539
So it’s great.

00:05:05.539 --> 00:05:06.919
Awesome that these films come to us.

00:05:06.919 --> 00:05:10.439
We know they made these festivals, all good.

00:05:10.439 --> 00:05:15.539
But everyone else is paying so…

00:05:15.539 --> 00:05:20.349
I know there are other circumstances where
there are other countries such as Iran comes

00:05:20.349 --> 00:05:25.349
up a lot, they cannot pay fees or there is
sanctions on credit cards that we hear about.

00:05:25.349 --> 00:05:29.161
I don’t know the political situation of
how this is fully accurate or not.

00:05:29.161 --> 00:05:31.449
I believe it is to be.

00:05:31.449 --> 00:05:33.210
We still get submission from Iran at times
and they pay.

00:05:33.210 --> 00:05:34.729
I don’t know how they do or with what?

00:05:34.729 --> 00:05:36.050
But they come in and they do.

00:05:36.050 --> 00:05:41.819
And those that don’t, we get emails from
there everyday probably five emails from there

00:05:41.819 --> 00:05:44.650
a day (maybe 10) asking for fee waivers.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.469
I can’t open the floodgates there.

00:05:46.469 --> 00:05:50.909
If I say yes and no one pays then all of these
films get to not pay but everyone else is

00:05:50.909 --> 00:05:51.909
paying.

00:05:51.909 --> 00:05:54.499
I’ve even asked people “Can someone else
pay for you?”

00:05:54.499 --> 00:05:58.809
There are other countries where people have
some money in the States or LA or whatever.

00:05:58.809 --> 00:06:00.210
Offer discounts or whatever, but it’s the
principal.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.580
If you’re just offering all of these waivers
for people.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:09.490
Now we have to spend our time and resources
for staff to watch these films, this doesn’t

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:10.490
work for us.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:12.460
I don’t see it as something that is fair.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:15.389
I know it is tough for those countries with
sanctions.

00:06:15.389 --> 00:06:20.180
That’s a tough situation but we haven’t
found a way to solve that.

00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.279
We’re just being honest.

00:06:22.279 --> 00:06:27.039
I know some festivals just completely waive
fees for Iran, feeling like they can’t pay

00:06:27.039 --> 00:06:28.879
and that kind of stuff.

00:06:28.879 --> 00:06:35.169
It’s not something we can do with our resources
and our team size.

00:06:35.169 --> 00:06:39.949
So we don’t, we’re not a proponent of
that and many times with the emails, if it’s

00:06:39.949 --> 00:06:47.009
not with any good effort…look people always
say “You get what you ask for.”

00:06:47.009 --> 00:06:48.009
You’ve got to ask.

00:06:48.009 --> 00:06:49.009
You don’t ask, you don’t receive.

00:06:49.009 --> 00:06:50.779
If you don’t ask and throw it out there,
why not?

00:06:50.779 --> 00:06:51.909
But if you do submit, fine.

00:06:51.909 --> 00:06:55.879
If you ask for a waiver and I say fine and
you don’t submit, now your film never plays

00:06:55.879 --> 00:06:58.860
and never gets in and what’s the point of
all that?

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.860
If you put that time into those emails, you
could put your time into something else.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:10.039
Film Courage: Well I’m not going to go into
the local coffee shop and say “Hey can you

00:07:10.039 --> 00:07:13.800
give me this one latte for free this time?”

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.800
Daniel: Exactly.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.669
To me there is nothing different.

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:21.740
I don’t even see how they can look at it
as anything different.

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:22.832
And that’s exactly the point.

00:07:22.832 --> 00:07:23.832
It’s a good analogy.

00:07:23.832 --> 00:07:27.979
You’re not going to walk into some store
and say “Give me this for free just because.”

00:07:27.979 --> 00:07:30.319
Whether we have struggled or not, everyone
has had some struggle.

00:07:30.319 --> 00:07:36.490
Again I was in position of real struggle in
college and you find a way to survive and

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:37.490
get by.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:41.199
You don’t just ask for things just because
you feel you’re in a different place or

00:07:41.199 --> 00:07:43.319
more special than anyone else or you don’t
want to pay just because you don’t want

00:07:43.319 --> 00:07:45.110
to.

00:07:45.110 --> 00:07:46.699
So those kind of emails I just don’t understand.

00:07:46.699 --> 00:07:49.212
You’re just basically telling me you just
don’t feel like paying so you’re going

00:07:49.212 --> 00:07:50.212
to ask.

00:07:50.212 --> 00:07:51.540
It’s really odd to me.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:54.370
If you think about any other business, like
if people all went to Starbucks and they had

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:57.520
10 people day all asking for a free cup of
coffee, it’s not happening.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:00.360
And imagine if it was and you’re like “No!”

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.330
It’s really a bizarre thing.

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:08.860
I guess it’s something that is like just
part of this business and it’s inherent

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:13.900
but it’s definitely different and unique
to this because Starbucks is not getting bombarded

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:18.909
every day with customers saying “Hey I want
this for free this time.”

00:08:18.909 --> 00:08:29.639
This is definitely a pet peeve for many festivals
and programmers I’d imagine (I’m speaking

00:08:29.639 --> 00:08:33.820
for others) Maybe some don’t care about
it much or like it but I’d imagine most

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:42.190
are not appreciative of emails all the time
spent on that…so definitely I’d say just

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:42.940
don’t.

